Project Mu: no Gemini in Chrome

Glic (Gemini in Chrome) is Google's AI assistant that reads the pages you
browse. It is on by default on Windows, and its component extension starts a
background worker in every profile even without a Google account. Mu turns
off both switches:

  * kGlic, the feature's own kill switch: no Gemini button, hotkey, panel
    or settings page.
  * kApiGlicPrivate: the built-in glic component extension is not loaded and
    its private API is not exposed.

(args.gn also sets disable_fieldtrial_testing_config, so experimental
studies such as contextual tasks and AI Mode stay at their defaults, off.)

diff --git a/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc b/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
index 4e871ad..2ca39ca 100644
--- a/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
+++ b/chrome/common/chrome_features.cc
@@ -525,14 +525,10 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kGlicMessageFirstFre, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 // IMPORTANT: this feature should never be expired! It is used as the main
 // kill-switch for Glic and can be used in the future to handle unsupported
 // Chrome versions.
-BASE_FEATURE(kGlic,
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
-    BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT
-#else
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT
-#endif
-);
+//
+// Project Mu: off everywhere. Glic is Gemini in Chrome, Google's AI assistant
+// that reads the pages you browse; it has no place in a private browser.
+BASE_FEATURE(kGlic, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kGlicBackgroundActuation, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
diff --git a/extensions/common/extension_features.cc b/extensions/common/extension_features.cc
index d0f9ea3..77f97fa 100644
--- a/extensions/common/extension_features.cc
+++ b/extensions/common/extension_features.cc
@@ -33,3 +33,5 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kApiContextualTasksPrivate, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kApiGlicPrivate, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// Project Mu: off, so Chromium's built-in glic (Gemini in Chrome) component
+// extension is not loaded and its API is not available.
+BASE_FEATURE(kApiGlicPrivate, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
